WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Tawanda Moyo grew up near Victoria Falls, surrounded by hard work and unconditional love. His father taught him to remember his roots. In time, a city job brought success, but calls grew shorter and visits became rare.

2
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:46.000
His parents sacrificed so he could study and build a future. When Tawanda left for the city, he promised to visit often. His father encouraged his ambition, asking only that he would always make time for home.

3
00:00:46.000 --> 00:01:08.000
City life brought promotions and new comforts. Back home, his parents invited him to the harvest festival. Tawanda put work first and missed it, telling himself there would always be another chance to see everyone.

4
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:31.000
During a visit, his father asked for his time, not just his financial support. Tawanda felt misunderstood and answered sharply. His mother tried to bridge the silence, but he returned to the city still postponing a proper conversation.

5
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:54.000
For his father’s seventieth birthday, Tawanda promised to come home. Then an important presentation fell on the same weekend. He chose work. His father accepted the news quietly, wondering whether the city was taking his son away.

6
00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:18.000
After a promotion, Tawanda celebrated with colleagues. His father called to discuss the farm and hear his voice. Meetings filled the day. Tawanda saw the missed calls and promised to call tomorrow, without realising how much that conversation mattered.

7
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Sekuru Moyo wrote down the things he hoped to discuss: family land, the future and his health. Tawanda declined another call during a meeting. Evening became night, and once again the conversation was left until tomorrow.

8
00:02:40.000 --> 00:03:02.000
Feeling unwell, Sekuru Moyo visited the clinic. He needed rest and support, and wished his son would come home. In the city, Thandi reminded Tawanda that time with parents was part of a meaningful life.

9
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:25.000
Sekuru Moyo wrote a loving letter, remembering his son’s childhood and wishing they could spend more time together. A voice message stirred Tawanda’s longing for home. Yet another urgent work commitment persuaded him to postpone his trip.

10
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:47.000
At last, Tawanda called and promised to visit. His father was delighted. But a rescheduled client meeting changed the plan again. As night fell in the village, another call was coming, one that would change everything.

11
00:03:47.000 --> 00:04:10.000
His mother called close to midnight. His father’s condition had worsened, and he needed hospital care. Tawanda packed immediately. At dawn he boarded a bus for home, hoping there was still time to listen, apologise and be present.

12
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:34.000
Mai Moyo welcomed him with tears. At the hospital, his father reached for his hand. Tawanda apologised for letting ambition create distance. His father reassured him of his love, and they began the conversation they had delayed for so long.

13
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:59.000
His father explained the plans for their land and farm: new crops, irrigation and opportunities for the community. Tawanda understood that the calls had been an invitation to share responsibility. He promised to support that vision and make time for his parents.

14
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:22.000
Back at the homestead, familiar fields and family photographs brought old memories to life. Tawanda reconnected with neighbours and relatives. Home became more than a place he had left behind; it was a source of belonging and purpose.

15
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:46.000
His father shared regrets of his own, and Tawanda began to see him more fully. Over a family meal, laughter returned. Tawanda could not recover the time he had missed, but he could choose how to use what remained.

16
00:05:46.000 --> 00:06:09.000
Sekuru Moyo passed on an old pocket watch from his own father. It stood for time, responsibility and a family legacy. Tawanda resolved to be present, strengthen the farm and help build a future for the community.

17
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:33.000
His father opened an old chest and spoke of a business opportunity he had once feared to pursue. Tawanda saw the dreams behind those regrets. He resolved to act with courage while also caring for the people who mattered.

18
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:57.000
While helping his mother, Tawanda found a letter about an old family land dispute and forgiveness. He understood how reconciliation had held their family together. He embraced his father and resolved to mend relationships, support the farm and move forward.

19
00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:22.000
Tawanda gathered the family to speak honestly and work together. Later, his childhood friend Rudo shared her work with young people in agriculture. Inspired, he planned a life that made room for work, family and community. Change would begin with his choices.
